# L §6.4: a scenario row "that overlaps a base row at the same keys says replace (LOAD-OVERLAP)", whatever the two
# rows' known dates (round 12b). The scenario's load is refused; the base answers alone (L §8.3).
=== hh.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-11-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input salary: money PLN

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  salary = 5 000.00 PLN "umowa"

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-11-01
  replace salary = 6 000.00 PLN "aneks"

ask b: salary law 2027-06-30
=== stop.tally
scenario stop over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version stop_salary
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  salary = 0 PLN "założenie"

ask s1: salary in stop law 2027-06-30
ask s2: salary in stop law 2026-06-30
=== expect
scenario stop: refused: LOAD-OVERLAP rows hh.tally:15 and stop.tally:9 of salary overlap at no keys, neither replacing the other (stop.tally:9)
b: 6 000.00 PLN
  held: salary = 6 000.00 PLN (v2), read for 2027-06-30
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2026-11-15
